From 6b765ff5ed49ab7109a1321da38d21698650ed82 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: genkigenki <3080081+genkigenki@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 19:19:51 +1000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] BLE attempt 69: the installer reads ctl.img back from the
 unit and compares the CRC32.

The editor has the new command 37 CTL_READ. It reads only the Bluetooth block (0x8B000, 64 KiB, FL_BLE).
CTL_READ does not write. An offset outside the block gets no reply. The count stops at the block end.
A static assert makes sure that XB_FLASH_OFF and XB_FLASH_SIZE are the same as FL_BLE_LO and FL_BLE_HI.
The command 36 (ABI 3 CTL2_READ) is not used. Thus an ABI 3 tool gets no reply.
ED_SMP_READ and CTL_READ use one packer, ed_put7. This keeps the app code small.
After the install, fm1_install.py reads the image back and prints the unit CRC32 and the file CRC32.
If the two CRC32 values are different or the unit does not answer, the installer stops with exit 8.
The installer reads back only if it added a ctl.img to the package.
The read-back comes after the slot restore. Thus a CRC32 error does not stop the slot restore.
tests/install_ctl_test.py checks the read-back, one changed bit, no reply and the bounds on a fake unit.
The flash map and tools/locked_settings.json do not change.
Not installed. Not tested on the unit.
